# Vercel ignore — only ship what Next.js needs.
# The Vercel upload has a 10MB body limit even for repo tarballs; this
# file keeps the deploy lean and fast. The repo IS the CMS (canon-fs.ts
# reads `bucket-canon/`), so canon directories MUST stay shipped — but
# the gigabytes of corpora, embeddings, archives, and intake data do not.

# Local corpora + intake — exclude the multi-GB subdirs but KEEP the
# small embedding / evidence / graph files that the runtime canon-search
# + canon-graph + canon-evidence libraries actually read at request time.
# (See src/lib/canon-search-index.ts and src/lib/canon-evidence.ts.)
_intake/photons/                      # 20 GB regenerable kaikki cache
_intake/war-gov-pursue-release-01/    # 2 GB war.gov mirror
_intake/aaro-mil-archive/             # 152 MB
_intake/training/                     # 132 MB
_intake/kruse-blog-corpus/            # 24 MB
_intake/claims-v2/
_intake/claims-allbranch/
_intake/dni-uap-reports/
_intake/canon-claims-raw/
_intake/kruse-references-mined/
_intake/concept-digests/
_intake/canon-profiles/
_intake/everychem/
_intake/gov-declassified/
# Per-figure / per-concept intake dirs (all near-empty placeholders).
# DO NOT use the lazy `_intake/*-*/` pattern here — it greedily matches
# `_intake/embeddings-v2/` (hyphenated), which BREAKS canon-search by
# stripping the precomputed claim vectors from the Lambda. The list
# below is enumerated explicitly so the next person who adds an
# `embeddings-v3/` or similar doesn't ship a search regression.
_intake/becker-robert-o/
_intake/einstein-albert/
_intake/faraday-michael/
_intake/ferry-david/
_intake/frohlich-herbert/
_intake/ling-gilbert/
_intake/marino-andrew/
_intake/maxwell-james-clerk/
_intake/mendeleev-dmitri/
_intake/mitchell-peter/
_intake/newton-isaac/
_intake/nordenstrom-bjorn/
_intake/peat-ray/
_intake/pollack-gerald/
_intake/popp-fritz-albert/
_intake/russell-walter/
_intake/szent-gyorgyi-albert/
_intake/tesla-nikola/
_intake/warburg-otto/
_intake/wheeler-john-archibald/
_intake/concept-circadian-light-environment/
_intake/concept-cmes-biology/
_intake/concept-deuterium-depleted-water/
_intake/concept-ez-water-fourth-phase/
_intake/concept-melanin-semiconductor/
_intake/concept-mitochondrial-chemiosmosis/
_intake/concept-photoelectric-effect-biology/
_intake/concept-quantum-biology/

# Inside _intake/embeddings/ the `corpus/` subdir is 304 MB of raw
# source documents that nothing at runtime needs — exclude it but keep
# the rest of the dir.
_intake/embeddings/corpus/

# Keep these explicitly (they're tiny and the runtime needs them):
#   _intake/embeddings/claims-vectors.f32.bin   (1.8 MB, fallback vectors)
#   _intake/embeddings/claim-evidence.jsonl     (5.4 MB, evidence per claim)
#   _intake/embeddings-v2/claims-vectors.npy    (899 KB, preferred vectors)
#   _intake/embeddings-v2/clusters.json
#   _intake/embeddings-v2/multi-branch-graph.json
#   _intake/connections/graph.json + centrality.json   (228 KB, /canon/graph)

yt/
archaeology/
openalex/
openalex-fanout/
openalex-citers/
arxiv/
pubmed/
gutenberg/
blog/

